{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/209092-werewolves-vs-demons","id":209092,"title":"Werewolves Vs. Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-25T22:55:09-07:00","id":209092,"title":"Werewolves Vs. Demons","content":"If you've been paying attention to the updates on the Idigam Chronicles, but the a Urathra are getting some very nice updating and streamlining of their systems and splats. As I was reading I was thinking that the WoD's most deadly predators versus its most resourceful and elusive spies would make for an <i>interesting</i> game of cat and mouse but...<br /> <br /> The two groups have few inherent conflicts of interest. The Forsaken, at last, tend towards the same territory (Cities) but other than that, they're not competing for resources, have different priorities, and want different things.<br /> <br /> So... can anyone give me any ideas on how to start a war?<br /> <br /> The only one that I can come up with is the one I've rejected: a false flag operation by a third party that gets them at each other s throats. I don't like that idea as it requires the involved parties to act like idiots: too much risk of railroading or the players derailing the plot. What are <i>legitimate</i> gripes that would get werewolves and demons to put knives at each others' throats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 09-17-2014, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T23:18:28-07:00","id":209124,"title":"","content":"An association of Tempters with designs on making a Hell out of the Shadow and a retinue of Saboteurs to incite the necessary spiritual disturbances in course of neutralizing Infrastructure. The wolf-changers marking one of the Unchained's higher-value connections for a Hunt. Mutually incompatible plans for the same territory.<br /> <br /> Also worth pointing out that werewolves, too, are at their least easy to detect in human form. The Uratha can play the cold-war game as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T23:19:28-07:00","id":209126,"title":"","content":"Easy: Territory.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are inherently territorial, and demons have to scrap for what they get, so pieces of suborned infrastructure are not going to be surrendered easily. Throw in the God Machine and spirits deliberately making things worse when they realize a conflict is a brewing and you got a nice turf war already set up.<br /> <br /> Also consider the value of people. Demons prey on humans in ways most Forsaken would have issues with, and werewolves hoard people demons might find desirable. None of that is touching on personal aspects, both of which demons and werewolves have reason to value dearly and fight for ferociously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T00:46:16-07:00","id":209179,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming the Pure are out of the question, but I imagine the Fire-Touched would gladly declare war against a bunch of perfect liars, on nothing but pure (Pure?) principle. Fallen angels versus the geas of heaven. Has a nice ring to it. It could certainly add another dimension to such a conflict, at least, if the Forsaken have the Anshega to consider as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T11:30:57-07:00","id":209437,"title":"","content":"You have to monkey with the setting assumptions a bit for this one, but what if Loci are actually Occult Matrices (or vice versa)? Think about it, they're basically both just Essence factories. The main differences are just who made them, and how they view the site. To the Uratha, they are sacred places created by manipulating the surrounding environment in such a way that it resonates with the desired emotion or concept, and then strengthen that resonance until it creates a wellspring of that energy. To the God-Machine, they are tools created by placing the proper infrastructure in the desired location so that, via natural processes, the location produces the desired output. Now, which party is right, and which party just happens to be using the right methods but misunderstanding why it works is a question for the ST. It could be that the Uratha prescribe false religious significance to what is basically just a process of creating the proper infrastructure. On the other hand, it could be that the God-Machine doesn't even realize what it's doing is a spiritual process, it's computer mind only understands that A + B = Essence. Maybe both are true to a certain extent. Either way, if the Unchained realize they can more safely harvest Aether at the Uratha's spiritual sites, and/or the Uratha realize the Unchaned have been stealing some kind of energy from &quot;naturally occurring&quot; Loci, you've got your reason to start a war right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T15:16:59-07:00","id":209542,"title":"","content":"Also its not necessarily human resources,... there only needs to be a piece of infrastructure inside the territory of the werewolfes and the demons have an interest for some reason in this piece of infrastructure. Werewolf won't like it that outsiders are tampering with something inside their territor or worse their home (the whole building they live in being the infrastructure)! If there is a saboteur who tries to take down the infrastructure or the demons saying the wrong thing at the wrong moment........things will get bloody quite fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","user":"Ryu","date":". 07-26-2014, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T16:32:22-07:00","id":209567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/209092-werewolves-vs-demons?p=209437#post209437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to monkey with the setting assumptions a bit for this one, but what if Loci are actually Occult Matrices (or vice versa)? Think about it, they're basically both just Essence factories. The main differences are just who made them, and how they view the site. To the Uratha, they are sacred places created by manipulating the surrounding environment in such a way that it resonates with the desired emotion or concept, and then strengthen that resonance until it creates a wellspring of that energy. To the God-Machine, they are tools created by placing the proper infrastructure in the desired location so that, via natural processes, the location produces the desired output. Now, which party is right, and which party just happens to be using the right methods but misunderstanding why it works is a question for the ST. It could be that the Uratha prescribe false religious significance to what is basically just a process of creating the proper infrastructure. On the other hand, it could be that the God-Machine doesn't even realize what it's doing is a spiritual process, it's computer mind only understands that A + B = Essence. Maybe both are true to a certain extent. Either way, if the Unchained realize they can more safely harvest Aether at the Uratha's spiritual sites, and/or the Uratha realize the Unchaned have been stealing some kind of energy from &quot;naturally occurring&quot; Loci, you've got your reason to start a war right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>With a little less monkeying, who says that the God-machine <i>is</i> a Essence factory? Angels are sustained by human cuts and ritual sacrifices(It's in GMC somewhere), not powered by a direct line to the God-Machine itself. It stands to reason that the God-Machine would hijack and use Loci for bigger projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T05:14:57-07:00","id":210023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/209092-werewolves-vs-demons?p=209567#post209567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a little less monkeying, who says that the God-machine <i>is</i> a Essence factory? Angels are sustained by human cuts and ritual sacrifices(It's in GMC somewhere), not powered by a direct line to the God-Machine itself. It stands to reason that the God-Machine would hijack and use Loci for bigger projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that works too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T15:47:02-07:00","id":210615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/209092-werewolves-vs-demons?p=209179#post209179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming the Pure are out of the question, but I imagine the Fire-Touched would gladly declare war against a bunch of perfect liars, on nothing but pure (Pure?) principle. Fallen angels versus the geas of heaven. Has a nice ring to it. It could certainly add another dimension to such a conflict, at least, if the Forsaken have the Anshega to consider as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was <i>hoping</i> to avoid using the Pure. I don't know how the Pure are handled in Idigam Chronicles, but if it follows the original vision, the Forsaken will be more heavily involved in cities, bringing them into conflict with the Unchained, and they have Auspices giving them more variety as adversaries.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the Pure end game (Pangaea restored, gauntlet dissolved) is <i>much</i> more hostile to Demonic interests than what the Forsaken seek. A conflict with the Forsaken means a grey-and-grey conflict where no side has the moral high ground by default. A three way conflict means that the Forsaken and Unchained can make common cause on a mutual enemy, creating the potential for creating common ground.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T16:11:22-07:00","id":210618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/209092-werewolves-vs-demons?p=210615#post210615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was <i>hoping</i> to avoid using the Pure. I don't know how the Pure are handled in Idigam Chronicles, but if it follows the original vision, the Forsaken will be more heavily involved in cities, bringing them into conflict with the Unchained, and they have Auspices giving them more variety as adversaries.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the Pure end game (Pangaea restored, gauntlet dissolved) is <i>much</i> more hostile to Demonic interests than what the Forsaken seek. A conflict with the Forsaken means a grey-and-grey conflict where no side has the moral high ground by default. A three way conflict means that the Forsaken and Unchained can make common cause on a mutual enemy, creating the potential for creating common ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re - Pure end-game: It's impossible to achieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T17:00:07-07:00","id":210649,"title":"","content":"True. But the damage they'll inflict trying is <i>very</i> achievable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T18:34:41-07:00","id":210689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/209092-werewolves-vs-demons?p=210649#post210649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. But the damage they'll inflict trying is <i>very</i> achievable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're confusing Pure with say, Beshilu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T18:52:53-07:00","id":210698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/209092-werewolves-vs-demons?p=210689#post210689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're confusing Pure with say, Beshilu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that. Destroying the Gauntlet in order to restore Pangaea is a common sentiment among the Pure. Many consider the Rat Hosts to be an ideal way of doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T02:16:56-07:00","id":210996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/209092-werewolves-vs-demons?p=210698#post210698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about that. Destroying the Gauntlet in order to restore Pangaea is a common sentiment among the Pure. Many consider the Rat Hosts to be an ideal way of doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the theory, but as it is, most are simply more preoccupied with hunting forsaken, as if when they're extinct the gauntlet would suddenly cease to exist with that accomplished. Rat Host can't be trusted.<br /> <br /> The Pure do allow spirits to run the show, get mounts, claim people and form cults. Tearing down the gauntlet? maybe when they're numerous enough and can wage war upon humanity and &quot;teach it its proper place&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}